@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "What is CI/CD?";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">CI/CD (Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment) is a methodology in DevOps that enables frequent and reliable code changes through automation.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- What is CI/CD? -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">Understanding CI/CD</h2>
        <p>
            CI/CD stands for Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (or Continuous Delivery). It is a set of practices that ensure software is developed, tested, and released efficiently, reducing manual intervention and increasing reliability.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/ci-cd-overview.jpg" alt="CI/CD Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>CI/CD automates the software development lifecycle.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Key Components of CI/CD -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Key Components of CI/CD</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Continuous Integration (CI):</strong> Developers integrate code into a shared repository multiple times a day, triggering automated builds and tests.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Continuous Deployment (CD):</strong> Automated deployment of tested code to production environments with minimal manual intervention.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Continuous Delivery:</strong> A process where code changes are automatically tested and prepared for release.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automation and Monitoring:</strong> CI/CD pipelines include automated testing, security checks, and monitoring tools.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/ci-cd-components.jpg" alt="Key Components of CI/CD" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>CI/CD consists of various automated processes to streamline development.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CI/CD Pipeline -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">CI/CD Pipeline Workflow</h2>
        <p>A typical CI/CD pipeline follows these steps:</p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Code is committed to a shared repository.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Automated build and unit tests are executed.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Code is reviewed and merged into the main branch.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Automated integration tests are performed.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Deployment to staging and then production environments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Monitoring and feedback mechanisms ensure continuous improvement.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/ci-cd-pipeline.jpg" alt="CI/CD Pipeline" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>A CI/CD pipeline ensures seamless integration and deployment of software.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Benefits of CI/CD -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Benefits of CI/CD</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Faster Development:</strong> Automating testing and deployment accelerates release cycles.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Higher Code Quality:</strong> Continuous testing reduces bugs and improves software stability.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Reduced Manual Effort:</strong> Automating repetitive tasks minimizes human errors.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Improved Collaboration:</strong> CI/CD fosters teamwork between developers and operations teams.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/ci-cd-benefits.jpg" alt="CI/CD Benefits" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>CI/CD improves efficiency, quality, and collaboration in software development.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            CI/CD is a crucial practice in modern software development, enabling teams to deliver high-quality software efficiently. By implementing CI/CD pipelines, organizations can achieve faster deployments, enhanced collaboration, and improved reliability.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/ci-cd-conclusion.jpg" alt="CI/CD Conclusion" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>CI/CD transforms software development by enhancing speed and reliability.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
